  data: {
    LLM: "Choose your partner wisely! Only accept a bid if you have the cards to support that suit. Since you are playing for your own score, don't help a partner who is significantly ahead of you in points unless you have to. If you are the Bidder, you want an Acceptor who holds the 'High Honors' (A-K-Q) in your suit.\n\nThe 'Partner Sabotage' (Defensive): If you are defending, you are not just trying to stop the contractâ€”you are trying to ensure the declarer (who is your rival in the overall game) doesn't gain points 'Below the Line'. Defending a 1-level contract is worth more to you psychologically than winning a 4-level contract yourself if it puts you in the lead.\n\nMarket Bidding: In Pirate Bridge, bidding is like a negotiation. If you bid 'One Heart' and no one accepts, your hand is 'Valueless'. You must learn to 'Invite' acceptance. Sometimes, bidding a slightly weaker suit that you know another player has 'Stop' in is better than bidding your longest suit that no one can help with. You need a partner to win.",
    Player: "Choose your partner wisely! Only accept a bid if you have the cards to support that suit. Since you are playing for your own score, don't help a partner who is significantly ahead of you in points unless you have to. If you are the Bidder, you want an Acceptor who holds the 'High Honors' (A-K-Q) in your suit.\n\nThe 'Partner Sabotage' (Defensive): If you are defending, you are not just trying to stop the contractâ€”you are trying to ensure the declarer (who is your rival in the overall game) doesn't gain points 'Below the Line'. Defending a 1-level contract is worth more to you psychologically than winning a 4-level contract yourself if it puts you in the lead.\n\nMarket Bidding: In Pirate Bridge, bidding is like a negotiation. If you bid 'One Heart' and no one accepts, your hand is 'Valueless'. You must learn to 'Invite' acceptance. Sometimes, bidding a slightly weaker suit that you know another player has 'Stop' in is better than bidding your longest suit that no one can help with. You need a partner to win.",
